{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00338","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00338@rel:R25-11#e0bc7dbf","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00338","release":"R25-11","content":"function ResetFile [SWS_PER_00338] Upstream: RS_PER_00001 , RS_PER_00004 , RS_PER_00009 , RS_AP_00119 , RS_AP_00120 , RS_AP_00121 , RS_AP_00127 , RS_AP_00128 , RS_AP_00129 , RS_AP_00135 , RS_AP_00139 , RS_AP_00159 ara::core::Result &lt; void &gt; ResetFile ( ara::core::StringView fileName) noexcept; Resets a file of this File Storage to its initial content. ResetFile allows to reset a single file to its initial content. If the file is currently not available in the File Storage, it is re-created. Afterwards, the file will appear in both cases as if it was newly installed from the current Target Configuration. It will fail with kResourceBusy when the file is currently open, and with kInitValueNotAvailable when neither Application Design nor Target Configuration define an initial content for the file. Header-Datei #include \"ara/per/file_storage.h\" class mono Scope class ara::per::FileStorage class mono Exception-Sicherheit exception safe class mono Thread-Sicherheit thread-safe PerErrc ::kPhysical no_rollback_semantics class mono Parameter (in) th Parameter th Beschreibung td fileName td File name of the file. May correspond to the PersistencyFile.file Name of a configured file. Rückgabewert th Typ th Beschreibung td ara::core::Result &lt; void &gt; td A Result of void. In case of an error, it contains any of the errors defined below, or a vendor specific error. Fehler th Fehlercode th Beschreibung td StorageFailure td Returned if access to the physical storage fails. td PerErrc ::kEncryptionFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the encryption or decryption of stored data fails. td PerErrc ::kInitValueNotAvailable td rollback_semantics Returned if no intitial value was configured for this file. td PerErrc ::kResourceBusy td rollback_semantics Returned if the file is open, or if DeleteFile or RecoverFile with the same file name is currently being executed. td PerErrc ::kOutOfStorageSpace td no_rollback_semantics Returned if the available physical storage space is insufficient for the initial file. td PerErrc ::kTooManyFiles td rollback_semantics Returned if the number of files would get larger than the configured maxNumberOfFiles when the file is restored. td PerErrc ::kQuotaExceeded td rollback_semantics Returned if the initial file would exceed the configured maximum AllowedSize of the File Storage. td PerErrc ::kAuthenticationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if calculating or checking the MAC of stored data fails.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"baseline_sync"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:43:34+00:00"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00338","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R25-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11"],"platform_releases":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11"},"element":{"kind":"function","name":"ResetFile","module":"PER","cluster":"","page":"classes/cl_ara_per_FileStorage_29266b.html","doc_type":"SWS","ai":false,"first":"R25-11","last":"R25-11","changed":[],"distinct":1,"universe":"AP"},"evidence":{"figures":[{"id":"FIG-90dbf15c08d6f936","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_EXP_SWArchitecture","p":87,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.85,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"ResetFile API in Persistency","n":9,"cap":"Figure 9.35: Interfaces for file storage","sha":"90dbf15c08d6f936c170554e8c7a2f77567241569f8f890405bc3996341e9929","nser":5,"src":"figure"},{"id":"SNIP_ADAPTIVE_PLATFORM_FIGURE_Figure_12_6","doc":"TPS_ManifestSpecification","p":561,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.75,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"Reset single file initial content","n":3,"cap":"Figure 12.6","sha":null,"nser":1,"src"